{t: The Sky Road (Leaving for America)}
{st:  composer: Jimmy MacCarthy, 1995}
{st: Produced by Arty McGlynn & Pearse Dunne; Performed by Frances Black }

Verse 1:
[F] Danny's made his mind up.  He's [Bb] leaving for America.
[F] He's leaving for America, Leaving all of us be [C] hind
He says there's [F] nothing here not drenched in beer
In [Bb] blood and retribution; And the [F] wealth's distribution's
Been weighing heavy on his [C] mind

Chorus 1:
And he [Dm] knows that he'll regret the leaving
[Dm6] Knows that he will pine for grieving
For the [Bb] sky road by the [F] singing sea
And all of us be [C] hind

Verse 2:
[F] Danny looks so lovely [Bb] working in the fields
Or [F] dancing like a wild one, Sparks flying around his [C] heels
But his [F] friends all gone before him
From the [Bb] sacred ground that bore them
Now they [F] wonder does she scorn them
For giving up the [C] land

Chorus 2:
And they [Dm] know that they'll regret the leaving
[Dm6] Know that they will pine for grieving
For the [Bb] sky road by the [F] singing sea
And all of us be [C] hind

Chorus 3:
And I [Dm] wonder does he know I love him
[Dm6] All below and none above him
As I [Bb] sit here by the [F] singing sea
Alone and left be [C] hind

{textcolour: blue}
